  "body": "The selected PR1094 R480 complex cleanup has no target-unread repeated-operand ADD corridor at any length. This package certifies all 111 repeated operand pairs with literal intervening-read witnesses and an independent backward read-epoch oracle. It closes a narrowly defined cancellation/combination class after a failed bounded pilot; it does not claim arbitrary cleanup optimality or a new kappa.\n\nThe unchanged 6,680-macro cleanup is independently priced against pinned PR696 primitive emission at 26,541 real-component / 53,082 complex primitives. Three planted profitable corridors are replayed on all rational basis columns, with a counterexample showing why reads matter. Seven semantic controls plus five packaging corruptions and minimal relocation exercise the certificate and source bindings under optimized Python.\n\nReproduce from the repository root:\n\n~~~text\npython -I -O -B research/complex-cleanup-corridors-seed28/verify.py\npython -I -O -B research/complex-cleanup-corridors-seed28/test_package.py\n~~~\n\nThe four consumed source pins bind the PR1042 archive reused by PR1094, actual slot receipt, selected-source binding and PR696 lowering. This is distinct from PR1119's historical U8 two-sided Markowitz refactor. Native/provider invoices, phases and precision admission are inherited and unexecuted. Contributor @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; full predecessor credit and Apache-2.0 included.\n",
